<title>POLAND: Espebepe falls 9.8 pct in profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Espebepe falls 9.8 pct in profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish builder Espebepe SA fell 9.8 percent to 8.75 zlotys in profit-taking after having surged this week on speculation that a March 14 creditors meeting might lead to a debt restructuring deal, traders said.</p>
<p>Espebepe, which has 80 million zlotys in debts, had gained 70 percent since February 18 before Friday's fall.</p>
<p>&quot;Only speculators buy such a stock,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Selling was strong enough after price-fixing for investors to have their bids reduced but analysts said there could still be more speculative rises before the creditors meet.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
